In this folder are python scripts that describe the general way of using the provided code to do the
KPM computations for the mass and bond disorder in parallel (ie each disorder realization running as its own process)

########################################################################################################################

Description of variables (For KPM_run_*.py scripts):

pval = the p that appears in the Schlafli symbol (here q=3 always)
nval = number of generations of hyperbolic lattice
(Important note: in the code the center plaquette generation is labelled 1 however in the papers we have put out
the convention is different, with the center plaquette generation being labelled as 0)

number_parallel_jobs = number of processes to run in parallel at a time
clean_hamiltonian = pristine, with no disorder {pval, 3} hyperbolic Dirac lattice hamiltonian
Wx_list (with x = m or b) = list of disorder strengths for the mass (x=m) or bond (x=b) disorder
num_moments = number of Chebyshev moments to compute up to
num_random_vectors = how many random vectors to use to do stochastic trace evaluation (basically always 12)
random_vector_dim = dimension of random vectors (set equal to number of sites)

eigenspectrum_min/max = the minimum and maximum bounds of the eigenspectrum
(if chosen poorly ie not enclosing whole spectrum then as job runs you will notice warnings in your terminal output)

save_directory = path to the directory where you want results to be saved into
save_name = a name for the saved files with the results
save_name_index_list = just a range of numbers, which are appended to end of save_name
(Because parallel jobs run and save to same directory, we need save_name_index_list to differentiate
save files and thus avoid overwriting)

rng_seeds = seed values which will define the rng for drawing the mass or band disorder
(Be sure for different runs to feed a different original_seed value in the run script)

########################################################################################################################

Description of variables (For Produce_ADOS_from_moments.py script):

data_directory = directory where moments data from KPM run are saved (the "save_directory" path in the run script)
data_name_template = name of the data files (change first part to the "save_name" string from run script
but keep '_{}' unchanged)
data_indices = list of all unique indices appended to end of file names (the "save_name_index_list" from run script)

energy_values = the energy values to sample when reproducing the ADOS from the moments
eigenspectrum_min/max = the eigenspectrum bounds specified in the run script (variables of same name in run script)






